    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.13 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWe can enter Insert mode with the `i` or `a` keys. I'd assume that `i` puts the cursor at the previous character, while `a` keeps it at the current character, since pressing `<Esc>` after `i` moves the cursor one character to the left.\n\nWhen using the `MiniAi` API from Insert mode after pressing `a`, the selection starts from the next character. This might be confusing because the same position in Normal mode selects a different range.\n\n*I guess the described behavior is arguable, but it's still worth considering.*\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51851c22-5ad9-4170-9517-52da08a6dc6d\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\n-- repro.lua\n\nvim.pack.add({\n  { src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\", version = \"main\" },\n})\n\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    w = { \"%w+\" },\n  },\n})\n\nvim.keymap.set({ \"i\", \"n\" }, \"<M-w>\", function()\n  MiniAi.select_textobject(\"i\", \"w\", { search_method = \"cover\" })\n  -- Off-topic: how to define a keymap to delete selected text?\nend, {})\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n-- i<Esc>i<Esc>i<Esc> -- Moves left\n-- a<Esc>a<Esc>a<Esc> -- Stays\n\n-- a<M-w>\n-- Reach me baby\n```",
