            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I've finally found time to take a closer look at this. It seems to work as expected, at least for these reasons:\n\n- The actual visual selection always includes the cursor cell. In case of Insert mode and bar cursor shape this is the cell to the right of the bar, no matter how the Insert mode was entered (with `a` or `i`).\n- When actually performing the action, it is done on the expected \"full\" action. For example, doing `<C-o>` - `d` will delete the expected selection.\n- This aligns with the behavior of the built-in textobjects. With the `:inorema <M-m> <Cmd>normal! viw<CR>`, pressing `<M-m>` also visually \"doesn't select\" the right edge, but it is in fact selected.",
